                    <h1 class="marginBottom20 ColorGreen">Copper Phthalocyanine Green</h1>
                    <p>Copper Phthalocyanine Green Pigment, also known as Pigment Green 7 (PG7), is a bright, brilliant green pigment widely recognized for its superior color strength, chemical stability, and versatility. It belongs to the family of phthalocyanine dyes and is created by chlorinating copper phthalocyanine blue, resulting in a complex organic compound with a vibrant green hue.</p>
                    <p>This pigment is a cornerstone in the pigment industry due to its high tinting strength, lightfastness, and resistance to heat, acids, and alkalis, making it suitable for a wide range of applications across industries.</p>
